{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119998","id":3797237443,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7iVT7D","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119998","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119998.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119998.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119998","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119998/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119998/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119998/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/15d8191fbfb7c274f0ad249d4938187504c6eb5b","number":119998,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"OpenGL: Fix vertex shader compilation error with `EYE_OFFSET`","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCurrently, if you use `EYE_OFFSET` in the `vertex()` function of a .gdshader on OpenGL, you'll get this error:\r\n\r\n```\r\n06-03 11:14:29.278  8841  8877 E godot   : ERROR: SceneShaderGLES3: Vertex shader compilation failed:\r\n06-03 11:14:29.278  8841  8877 E godot   : ERROR: 0:804: 'eye_offset' : undeclared identifier\r\n06-03 11:14:29.278  8841  8877 E godot   : ERROR: 0:804: 'xy' :  field selection requires structure, vector, or matrix on left hand side\r\n06-03 11:14:29.278  8841  8877 E godot   : ERROR: 2 compilation errors.  No code generated.\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn XR, the shader will still work - this error is from compiling the non-multiview variant where `eye_offset` isn't defined, but it will be there in the multiview variant\r\n\r\nThe issue is that we should always make sure that `eye_offset` is defined, which is already handled for the fragment shader on OpenGL, and for both the vertex and fragment shaders in the Mobile and Forward+ renderers.\r\n\r\nIt was just omitted for the vertex shader in OpenGL, which is what this PR fixes :-)","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/label